  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (multimodal, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieved 0.532 acc, only marginally above RNA-alone scvi_n200 (0.520), while image-alone was very weak (0.227). This suggests the RNA encoder is the dominant signal source and the image contributes little. Uncertainty: we have only tested one RNA encoder (scvi_n200); it is unknown whether scgpt produces a more informative representation that could raise the ceiling. Question: config_023 changes exactly one variable relative to config_002 (RNA encoder scvi_n200 → scgpt) while holding model_setting, profile_setting, image_encoder, aggregation, and fusion constant. This cleanly isolates the effect of the RNA representation. Why best next: the RNA encoder is the highest-leverage design choice given that RNA drives most of the signal; a single-variable comparison against our current best (config_002) maximizes information per experiment and avoids confounding with fusion or image-encoder changes. If scgpt substantially outperforms scvi_n200, it redirects the search toward scgpt-based configurations; if not, it confirms scvi_n200 is adequate and we can pivot to fusion or profile-setting questions."
}

